*In the early 11th century {{CE}} {{ltc-l|瀧|tr= sraewng}} ({{w|Baxter's transcription for Middle Chinese|Baxter}}) already possessed retroflex fricative initial (as indicated by pronunciation {{lang|zh|所江切}} in ''{{w|Guangyun}}'' {{defdate|1007 - 1008 {{CE}}}}); meanwhile, 
*Nôm transcriptions in the 12th-century ''{{lang|vi|Phật thuyết đại báo phụ mẫu ân trọng kinh}}'' ({{lang|zh|佛說大報父母恩重經}}) demonstrate that Old Vietnamese then still retained clusters {{IPAfont|*/Cr-/}}, which would not become a retroflex fricative ancestral to Modern Vietnamese ‹s-› {{IPAfont|/ʂ ~ s/}} until much later.

